  He barely moves; FIS moves ~(1-F)/F times as much, because FIS divides by
  the small quantity the two estimators disagree about. So Stacks' Pi is safe
  to quote and its Fis is not (and its Fis carries a second, larger error:
  it is a mean of per-locus ratios).
  Compare against `Pi`, never `Exp_Het`: Pi = Exp_Het * 2n/(2n-1) = x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.030 at n=17, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20, x1.026 at n=20.
  -> MINIMAL_WORKFLOW.md, "Formulas, and what maps onto what in Stacks"

